title: Palm Sunday
subtitle: 13 April. Bamberg's putsch fails, and Munich turns to us.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: crisis_bavaria = 1 and crisis_time = 1
max-visits: 1

= Palm Sunday

Before dawn on Palm Sunday, 13 April, the Republican Guard, loyal to Hoffmann, arrested Mühsam and a dozen council leaders and declared the council republic over. By evening armed workers and soldiers had stormed the main station and driven the Guard out of the city. It was the Communists who led the fight.

That night the factory and barracks councils meet in the Hofbräuhaus. They depose the Central Council and offer power to an Executive Council of fifteen, with Leviné at its head. Leviné hesitates. [? if levi_chair = 1 : In Berlin, Levi thinks a soviet republic in a Catholic, peasant Bavaria, alone, is doomed. ?][? if levi_chair = 0 : In Berlin, the Zentrale fears that a soviet Bavaria, alone, is doomed. ?] But Munich's workers are armed and waiting, and they expect an answer tonight.

- @take: Take power. Leviné leads the Executive Council.
- @coalition: Share power with the Independents and Toller.
- @defend: Defend the councils, but refuse the government.

@take
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's answer: the second soviet republic in Europe, after Hungary. The responsibility will be ours alone.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids seizing power.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.bav_power = 1;
Q.crisis_momentum += 15;
Q.militancy += 10;
Q.repression += 6;
Q.world_revolution += 5;
Q.district_bavaria_members += 1.0;
Q.district_bavaria_loyalty += 10;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 12;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 4;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
!}

Leviné accepts. The Executive Council orders a general strike against Bamberg, the disarming of the bourgeoisie and the formation of a Red Army. Rudolf Egelhofer, a sailor of twenty-three, takes command of it.

@coalition
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's answer: a broader government, and a broader base.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids sharing power with social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.bav_power = 3;
Q.crisis_momentum += 8;
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.district_bavaria_members += 0.6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 8;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

The Executive Council takes in Independents and Toller's friends. It argues more and decides less, but the Munich Independents now stand and fall with us.

@defend
subtitle: The Spartacist line. The Communists defend the workers, and keep out of a doomed government.
on-arrival: bav_power = 2; crisis_momentum += 2; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6; offensive_satisfaction -= 6; lean_luxemburgist += 2; district_bavaria_loyalty -= 4

Leviné tells the Hofbräuhaus that the party will fight in the ranks but will not govern. The councils form a weaker executive without us. Some of our own people call it cowardice.
